hadiths[34]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1405","Sufyan told us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When there was revealed: Then you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, along with our disputing in this world. He said: Yes. And when there was revealed: Then you will surely be questioned that Day about bliss, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss will we be questioned about, when they are only the two black things, dates and water. He said: Indeed that will surely be."
"1406","Sufyan told us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws: I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say to Abd al-Rahman and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Sad: I adjure you by Allah by Whom heaven and earth stand, and Sufyan once said: by Whose permission they stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. He said: They said: O Allah, yes."
"1407","Hafs ibn Ghiyath told us, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For a man to carry a rope and gather firewood with it, then come and place it in the market and sell it, then become independent by it and spend it on himself, is better for him than to ask people, whether they give him or withhold from him."
"1408","Abu Muawiyah told us: Hisham told us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, joined for me both his parents on the Day of Uhud."
"1409","Abu Usamah told us: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: When it was the Day of the Trench, I and Umar ibn Abi Salamah were in the fortress in which were the women of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the fortress of Hassan. He would lift me and I would lift him, and when he lifted me I recognized my father when he passed toward Banu Qurayzah, and he was fighting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the Day of the Trench. Then he said: Who will go to Banu Qurayzah and fight them. Then I said to him when he returned: O father, by Allah I indeed recognized you when you passed going toward Banu Qurayzah. Then he said: O my son, indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would join for me both his parents together, ransoming me with them, saying: May my father and my mother be ransom for you."
"1410","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that a man mounted a mare called Ghamrah or Ghamra, and he said: Then he found a horse or a foal for sale, and it was attributed to that mare, and he was forbidden from it."
"1411","Yazid told us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then depart and hasten to the thickets, and we would find only the space of our feet. Yazid said: The thickets are the fortresses."
"1412","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, and Abu Muawiyah Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: envy and hatred, and hatred is the shaver, the shaver of religion, not the shaver of hair. And by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of something which if you do it you will love one another: Spread peace among you."
"1413","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I said to al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him: Why do I not hear you narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as I hear Ibn Masud and so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: Indeed I have not parted him since I embraced Islam, but I heard from him a statement: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1414","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: Shaddad, meaning Ibn Said, told us: Ghaylan ibn Jarir told us, from Mutarrif, he said: We said to al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him: O Abu Abdullah, what has brought you; you neglected the caliph until he was killed, then you came seeking his blood. Al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We used to recite it in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them: And fear a trial which will not only befall those who wronged among you especially. We did not think that we were its people until it fell from us where it fell."
"1415","Muhammad ibn Kunasah told us: Hisham ibn Urwah told us, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Change grey hair and do not resemble the Jews."
"1416","Abdullah ibn al-Harith of the people of Makkah, a Makhzumi, told us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Insan narrated to me, he said, and he praised him well, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a night journey until when we were at al-Sidrah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at the edge of the black mountain opposite it, and faced Nakhib with his sight, meaning a valley, and stood until all the people gathered. Then he said: The game of Wajj and its thorny trees are a sanctuary made sacred for Allah. And that was before his coming down to Taif and his besieging Thaqif."
"1417","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from Ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say on that day: Talhah has earned it, when he did with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what he did, meaning when Talhah knelt for him and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, climbed upon his back."
"1418","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad, informed us, from Hisham, from Urwah, he said: My father al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that when it was the Day of Uhud, a woman came hurrying until when she was almost to overlook the slain, he said: Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked that she see them, and said: The woman, the woman. Al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I thought that she was my mother Safiyyah. He said: So I went out hurrying to her and reached her before she reached the slain. He said: Then she struck my chest, and she was a strong woman. She said: Away from me, may you have no ground. He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has adjured you. He said: So she stopped, and brought out two garments with her, and said: These are two garments I brought for my brother Hamzah, for I have heard of his killing, so shroud him in them. He said: So we brought the two garments to shroud Hamzah in them, and there beside him was a slain man from the Ansar to whom had been done as had been done to Hamzah. He said: So we felt reluctance and shyness to shroud Hamzah in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud. So we said: For Hamzah one garment and for the Ansari one garment. Then we measured them, and one of them was larger than the other, so we cast lots between them, and shrouded each one of them in the garment that fell to him."
"1419","Abu al-Yaman told us: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, used to narrate that he disputed with a man from the Ansar who had witnessed Badr, before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the streams of al-Harrah from which they both irrigated. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him: Irrigate, then send on to your neighbor. Then the Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is the son of your aunt. Then the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed color. Then he said to al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him: Irrigate, then hold back the water until it returns to the wall. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the full right for al-Zubayr at that time, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, before that had pointed al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, to an opinion in which he intended latitude for him and for the Ansari. Then when the Ansari angered the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the full right for al-Zubayr in plain judgment. Urwah said: Then al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, I do not think this verse was revealed except about that: No, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what has disputed between them, then find in themselves no distress in what you have decreed, and submit fully."
"1420","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi told us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us: Jubayr ibn Amr al-Qurashi narrated to me: Abu Sad al-Ansari narrated to me, from Abu Yahya, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The lands are the lands of Allah and the servants are the servants of Allah, so wherever you find good, settle."
"1421","Yazid told us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us: Jubayr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Sad al-Ansari, from Abu Yahya, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at Arafah, reciting this verse: Allah witnesses that there is no god but He, and the angels and those of knowledge, upholding justice; there is no god but He, the Mighty, the Wise. And I am among the witnesses to that, O Lord."
"1422","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Abdullah ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from his mother and his grandmother Umm Ata, they both said: By Allah, it is as if we are looking at al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, when he came to us on a white mule of his and said: O Umm Ata, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has forbidden the Muslims to eat from the meat of their sacrifices beyond three days. He said: So I said: May my father be for you, then how do we do with what was gifted to us. Then he said: As for what was gifted to you, do with it as you wish."
"1423","Attab ibn Ziyad told us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, told us: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: On the Day of the Confederates I and Umar ibn Abi Salamah were placed with the women. Then I looked, and there was al-Zubayr on his horse going back and forth to Banu Qurayzah two or three times. When he returned I said: O father, I saw you going back and forth. He said: Did you see me, O my son. He said: I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who will go to Banu Qurayzah and bring me their news. So I went, and when I returned the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, joined for me both his parents and said: May my father and my mother be ransom for you."
"1424","Attab told us: Abdullah told us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uqbah, and he is Abdullah ibn Lahiah ibn Uqbah, informed us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from one who heard Abdullah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah say: I heard Sufyan ibn Wahb al-Khawlani say: When we conquered Egypt without a treaty, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: O Amr ibn al-As, divide it. Amr said: I will not divide it. Then al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, you shall divide it as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided Khaybar. Amr said: By Allah, I will not divide it until I write to the Commander of the Believers. So he wrote to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar wrote to him: Leave it settled until the offspring of offspring raid from it."
"1425","Attab told us: Abdullah told us: Fulayh ibn Muhammad told us, from al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave al-Zubayr one share, and his mother one share, and his horse two shares."
"1426","Affan told us: Mubarak told us: al-Hasan told us, he said: A man came to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and said: Shall I kill Ali for you. He said: No, and how would you kill him while the troops are with him. He said: I will join him and assassinate him. He said: No, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Faith restrains assassination; a believer does not assassinate."
"1427","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us: al-Hasan told us, he said: A man came to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and said: Shall I not kill Ali for you. He said: And how can you kill him while the people are with him. Then he mentioned its meaning."
"1428","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us: Shubah told us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I said to my father al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him: Why do you not narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I have not parted him since I embraced Islam, but I heard from him a statement; I heard him say: Whoever lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1429","Waki and Ibn Numayr both said: Hisham ibn Urwah told us, from his father, from his grandfather, Ibn Numayr said: from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For one of you to take his ropes and come to the mountain and bring a bundle of firewood on his back and sell it and become independent by its price is better for him than to ask people, whether they give him or withhold from him."
"1430","Abd al-Rahman told us: Harb ibn Shaddad told us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Yaish ibn al-Walid narrated to him, that a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr narrated to him, that al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: envy and hatred, and hatred is the shaver; I do not say it shaves hair, but it shaves religion. And by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, or: by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of what will establish that for you: Spread peace among you."
"1431","Abu Amir told us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak told us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid, that a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr narrated to him, that al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There has crept to you, then he mentioned it."
"1432","Ibrahim ibn Khalid told us: Rabah told us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, from a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, that al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There has crept to you, then he mentioned it."
"1433","Ismail told us: Ayyub told us, from al-Hasan, he said: A man said to al-Zubayr: Shall I not kill Ali for you. He said: How would you kill him. He said: I will assassinate him. He said: No. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Faith restrains assassination; a believer does not assassinate."
"1434","Ibn Numayr told us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, told us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: When this chapter was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: You will die and they will die, then you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will there be repeated upon us what was between us in this world along with the particular sins. He said: Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every one with a right is given his right. Then al-Zubayr said: By Allah, the matter is severe."
"1435","Sufyan told us, he said: Amr, and I heard Ikrimah: And when We turned toward you, and it was recited to Sufyan, from al-Zubayr, a group of the jinn listening to the Quran, he said: At Nakhlah, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying the last evening prayer, they almost crowded upon him in masses. Sufyan said: Some of them were upon others like felted masses, some upon others."
"1436","Yahya ibn Adam told us: Ibn Abi Dhib told us: Muslim ibn Jundub told us: One who heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he says: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then hasten, and we would find of shade only the space of our feet, or he said: So we would not find of shade the space of our feet."
"1437","Kathir ibn Hisham told us: Hisham told us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Salamah or Maslamah, Kathir said, and my memory is Salamah, from Ali or from al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to address us and remind us of the days of Allah until we would recognize that in his face, as if he were a warner of a people whom the matter would come upon in the morning, and when he had lately been with Gabriel he would not smile laughing until it had lifted from him."
"1438","Aswad ibn Amir told us: Jarir told us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, he said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said: This verse was revealed while we were numerous with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: And fear a trial which will not only befall those who wronged among you especially. Then we kept saying: What is this trial, and we did not feel that it would fall where it fell. End of the hadith of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
